                        <field name="dc_description">The anonymous hymn of praise to the Creator Perek schira has been preserved in hundreds of manuscripts. Most of the important 18th-century Hebrew book illustrators illustrated the hymn. This manuscript was written for Hertz ben Leib Darmstadt of Frankfurt am Main and contains pen drawings by Meshullam Zimmel ben Moses from Polna/Bohemia; however, he probably produced this manuscript in Vienna. </field>
